<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>
        <version>3.5.16</version>
        <relativePath/>
    </parent>

    <groupId>br.com.aguas</groupId>
    <artifactId>aguas-api</artifactId>
    <version>1.1.0</version>
    <name>aguas-api</name>
    <description>API REST do sistema Águas do Capibaribe (gestão de consumo de água)</description>

    <properties>
        <java.version>25</java.version>
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
        <!-- Versões acima das do Spring Boot 3.5.16, para corrigir vulnerabilidades apontadas pelo OSV-Scanner
             (job "dependencias" do CI). Remover quando o Spring Boot trouxer versões iguais ou mais novas. -->
        <tomcat.version>10.1.61</tomcat.version>
        <postgresql.version>42.7.14</postgresql.version>
        <jackson-bom.version>2.21.8</jackson-bom.version>
        <!-- Disjuntor dos envios ao Telegram. A linha 2.x é a de Java 17+ e Spring Boot 3.x. -->
        <resilience4j.version>2.3.0</resilience4j.version>
    </properties>

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-jpa</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-validation</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-security</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <!-- Validação e emissão de JWT (Nimbus), sem biblioteca extra -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-oauth2-resource-server</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <!-- Saúde e métricas da API em /api/actuator/health e /api/actuator/metrics (issue #51) -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-actuator</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <!-- Limite de requisições no login e no registro de lotes (issue #60) -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.bucket4j</groupId>
            <artifactId>bucket4j_jdk17-core</artifactId>
            <version>8.22.0</version>
        </dependency>
        <!-- Documentação interativa (Swagger UI) em /api/swagger-ui.html; linha 2.8 = Spring Boot 3.x -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springdoc</groupId>
            <artifactId>springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui</artifactId>
            <version>2.8.17</version>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.postgresql</groupId>
            <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
            <scope>runtime</scope>
        </dependency>
        <!-- Migrações do esquema (src/main/resources/db/migration), aplicadas ao subir a API -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
            <artifactId>flyway-core</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
            <artifactId>flyway-database-postgresql</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Disjuntor (circuit breaker) dos envios ao Telegram (issue #52): com o Telegram fora do ar, as chamadas
             seguintes são recusadas na hora, sem esperar o tempo limite da rede. Só o núcleo da biblioteca, usado
             direto no código (Telegram.enviar); não entra o starter com AOP e anotações. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>io.github.resilience4j</groupId>
            <artifactId>resilience4j-circuitbreaker</artifactId>
            <version>${resilience4j.version}</version>
        </dependency>
        <!-- Estado e contagens do disjuntor em /api/actuator/metrics (resilience4j.circuitbreaker.*). -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>io.github.resilience4j</groupId>
            <artifactId>resilience4j-micrometer</artifactId>
            <version>${resilience4j.version}</version>
        </dependency>

        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-security-test</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-testcontainers</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
            <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
            <!-- Cobertura de testes (issue #168): o JaCoCo mede, no mvn test, quais linhas e decisões os testes executam.
                 Relatório em target/site/jacoco (index.html para ler, jacoco.xml para o SonarQube). -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.jacoco</groupId>
                <artifactId>jacoco-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>0.8.16</version>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>agente</id>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>prepare-agent</goal>
                        </goals>
                    </execution>
                    <execution>
                        <id>relatorio</id>
                        <phase>test</phase>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>report</goal>
                        </goals>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
            <!-- SBOM (issue #169): lista de todas as dependências, inclusive as transitivas, com hashes e licenças,
                 no padrão CycloneDX. O Spring Boot já gera um SBOM em JSON dentro do jar (META-INF/sbom); esta
                 execução gera também os arquivos publicados pelo CI: target/bom.json e target/bom.xml. -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.cyclonedx</groupId>
                <artifactId>cyclonedx-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>2.9.3</version>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>sbom-arquivos</id>
                        <phase>package</phase>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>makeBom</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <configuration>
                            <projectType>application</projectType>
                            <schemaVersion>1.6</schemaVersion>
                            <outputFormat>all</outputFormat>
                            <outputName>bom</outputName>
                            <outputDirectory>${project.build.directory}</outputDirectory>
                            <!-- Só o que vai para a imagem: dependências de teste ficam fora. -->
                            <includeTestScope>false</includeTestScope>
                            <skipAttach>true</skipAttach>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
            <!-- Migrações sem subir a API: mvn flyway:info / flyway:migrate (conexão em FLYWAY_URL,
                 FLYWAY_USER e FLYWAY_PASSWORD; ver database/LEIA-ME.md). Versão do Spring Boot. -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
                <artifactId>flyway-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>${flyway.version}</version>
                <configuration>
                    <locations>
                        <location>filesystem:src/main/resources/db/migration</location>
                    </locations>
                    <baselineVersion>4</baselineVersion>
                    <baselineDescription>esquema do banco.sql com auditoria</baselineDescription>
                    <cleanDisabled>true</cleanDisabled>
                </configuration>
                <dependencies>
                    <dependency>
                        <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
                        <artifactId>flyway-database-postgresql</artifactId>
                        <version>${flyway.version}</version>
                    </dependency>
                    <dependency>
                        <groupId>org.postgresql</groupId>
                        <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
                        <version>${postgresql.version}</version>
                    </dependency>
                </dependencies>
            </plugin>
            <!-- Usado só para a ferramenta de geração de hash BCrypt (ver README) -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.codehaus.mojo</groupId>
                <artifactId>exec-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.5.0</version>
                <configuration>
                    <mainClass>br.com.aguas.ferramentas.GerarHashSenha</mainClass>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>
            <!-- Teste de mutação (PIT): mvn test-compile org.pitest:pitest-maven:mutationCoverage
                 Muda o código das regras de negócio, da segurança e dos avisos e confere se algum teste falha.
                 Usa todos os testes, inclusive os de integração (precisa de Docker, como o mvn test).
                 Relatório em target/pit-reports/index.html. Ver docs/tecnico/testes.md. -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.pitest</groupId>
                <artifactId>pitest-maven</artifactId>
                <version>1.25.9</version>
                <dependencies>
                    <dependency>
                        <groupId>org.pitest</groupId>
                        <artifactId>pitest-junit5-plugin</artifactId>
                        <version>1.2.3</version>
                    </dependency>
                </dependencies>
                <configuration>
                    <targetClasses>
                        <param>br.com.aguas.service.*</param>
                        <param>br.com.aguas.security.*</param>
                        <param>br.com.aguas.notificacao.*</param>
                    </targetClasses>
                    <targetTests>
                        <param>br.com.aguas.*</param>
                    </targetTests>
                    <threads>4</threads>
                    <!-- Cada processo do PIT sobe o Spring e o PostgreSQL de teste de novo: sem esta folga,
                         a subida seria contada como demora do mutante (falso "morto por tempo"). -->
                    <timeoutConstant>60000</timeoutConstant>
                    <outputFormats>
                        <param>HTML</param>
                        <param>XML</param>
                    </outputFormats>
                    <timestampedReports>false</timestampedReports>
                    <!-- Mutantes mortos em pelo menos 81%: sobrevivência (com os sem cobertura) abaixo de 20%. -->
                    <mutationThreshold>81</mutationThreshold>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
